    <!-- ================================================================================
         Weapon/armor LEVEL scaling reach: add the base fliers + Thor/SiegeTank +
         Medivac/Raven + the elite mercs (MercThor/MercHellion/MercWraith) to the base
         Terran{Ship,Vehicle}{Weapons,Armors}LevelN upgrades that the Eng Bay sync grants.

         WHY: WoL splits weapon/armor research into TWO upgrade families per level:
           * the BASE  Terran{Ship,Vehicle}{Weapons,Armors}LevelN  ids, and
           * the WRAPPER …UltraCapacitorsLevelN / …VanadiumPlatingLevelN ids.
         Our sync (libWoLU_SyncWeaponArmorLevels) grants ONLY the base-Level ids (they
         carry the real effects; the wrappers are icon-only display variants). But the
         base-Level upgrades' EffectArrays MISS several player combat units — Banshee,
         Battlecruiser, Viking, Medivac, Raven, base Thor/SiegeTank armor, and the elite
         mercs — whose scaling entries live ONLY in the …UltraCapacitors/…VanadiumPlating
         WRAPPERS (liberty.sc2campaign/UpgradeData.xml: TerranShipWeaponsUltraCapacitors
         :394, TerranVehicleArmorsVanadiumPlating :318, TerranShipArmorsVanadiumPlating
         :467). The sync never grants those wrappers, so those units did not scale with
         the player's research. (Wraith, Hercules, the standalone fliers/mercs, and all
         ground vehicle weapons + Odin ALREADY have base-Level entries — verified — so
         they are intentionally NOT re-stated below.)

         FIX: a same-id <CUpgrade> here MERGES onto the vanilla definition; NEW Reference=
         keys in an EffectArray APPEND (the CombatShield/MarauderLifeBoost pattern above —
         no explicit index= for new keys). Below we append ONLY the missing unit keys,
         mirroring the wrapper Values exactly. We deliberately OMIT the wrappers'
         LifeMax/LifeStart ×1.05 Multiply entries — that +5% HP perk is separate from the
         armor-LEVEL scaling, and the base-Level upgrades carry only LifeArmor+LifeArmorLevel.

         MERC REACH (rule 4): armor is a per-unit-id Unit field, so it does NOT reach a
         parent= merc — MercThor/MercHellion/MercWraith need explicit Unit entries (added).
         Weapons reach parent= mercs via shared effect ids, so no merc-weapon entry is
         needed. Standalone mercs/heroes already have their own base-Level entries (verified).

         RULE 9: this is a global EffectArray edit, but (a) owner-approved, (b) same risk
         class as the base-Wraith coverage already present in these upgrades, (c) the
         player gets these upgrades per-player via the sync — enemies scale only if a
         mission grants them that exact base-Level upgrade, which WoL does not.

         IN-GAME VERIFY ITEM (single): our mod reroutes the Viking ground weapon
         TwinGatlingCannon's Effect to TwinGatlingCannonsWoLUSet (children parent=
         "TwinGatlingCannons"); whether the upgrade's Effect,TwinGatlingCannons,Amount bump
         propagates to the already-loaded child clones is unverified statically — but this
         is the SAME class as the shipped Thor case (vehicle-weapon upgrade modifies
         Effect,ThorsHammerDamage,Amount while the Thor weapon is rerouted to a *WoLUSet
         with children parent="ThorsHammerDamage"), which works per owner. Mirroring it is
         consistent with that precedent. Flag Viking-ground-damage-scaling for playtest.
         ================================================================================ -->

